cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this guide in your work, please cite it as below.
title: "LLM-Assisted Bioimage Analysis: Worked Examples"
abstract: >-
  An open guide of worked examples teaching biologists how to use large
  language models (LLMs) for microscopy image analysis reproducibly. Each
  example contrasts a tempting, unreproducible approach with asking the LLM
  to write a script that can be inspected, shared and rerun.
type: generic
authors:
  - family-names: Barry
    given-names: David J
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2763-5244"
    affiliation: "The Francis Crick Institute, London, UK"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FrancisCrickInstitute/reproducible-ia-with-ai"
url: "https://franciscrickinstitute.github.io/reproducible-ia-with-ai/"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
keywords:
  - image analysis
  - microscopy
  - bioimage analysis
  - reproducibility
  - large language models
  - Python
  - Quarto
  - Cellpose
